# Strategic Batching

Strategic batching is a workflow design method that groups similar tasks together to minimize context-switching and maximize efficiency. It is a core technique within the slow productivity framework.

## How It Works

Instead of switching between different types of work throughout the day, strategic batching clusters related tasks into dedicated blocks. This reduces the cognitive cost of switching mental modes and allows deeper engagement with each type of work.

## Application

- Grouping email processing into specific windows rather than checking constantly
- Batching meetings on specific days
- Consolidating administrative tasks into single sessions
- Protecting blocks for deep, focused creative or analytical work

## Benefits

- Reduces interruption frequency
- Enables deeper engagement per task type
- Lowers cognitive switching costs
- Supports the transition into deep focus states

